# Commits the lane rule forgives BY NAME. One sha per line, reason after it.
# See AGENTS.md, "Classifying a change".
#
# WHY A LIST AND NOT A MOVING CUTOFF. tools/commit_lane.since is a single sha
# and exempts everything at or before it, forever. That is the right shape for
# "the rule starts here" and the wrong shape for "these six specific commits".
# Advancing .since past 8e6707d would grandfather all 49 commits behind it and
# gut the check. This file names each forgiven commit individually, so a future
# miss BELOW them still fails. Tracked as bd inc-3aqd.
#
# WHY THESE SIX WERE NOT SIMPLY REWORDED. The oldest is 04431f2, from
# 2026-09-02, so rewording rewrites 49 commits and needs a force-push. Four
# things break:
#
#   - the `beta` tag contains 04431f2 and is the Steam Deck prerelease the
#     Ally installs from;
#   - five in-tree citations name shas in the range --
#     docs/specs/2026-09-02-demo-level-brief.md:37 and tools/nightly_verify.sh:29
#     name 04431f2, docs/specs/2026-09-03-fog-brief.md:15 names 0654a25,
#     tools/keys/light-fog.keys:20 and tools/keys/lightfilter-show.keys:34
#     name cab4cd3;
#   - beads reference 04431f2 and 0747c0c, and those sync to the public tracker;
#   - the Ally session's clone would need a hard reset.
#
# Rewriting published history is a worse harm than a wrong subject prefix.
# Leaving the check red is worse than both: a check that stays red is a check
# people stop reading.
#
# THE LIST IS CLOSED AT SIX. c7e5d2f added .beads/hooks/commit-msg, which
# refuses an invalid subject before the commit exists, so no new laneless
# commit can be created. Adding a seventh line here should be very hard to
# justify; prefer rewording anything not yet pushed.
#
# Full 40-character shas, so a short-sha collision can never silently forgive
# the wrong commit.

8e6707db347efa78051a2c4f2bb5d71ef87b03c6  2026-09-05  data: item and feat corrections. "Paladins wield holy; Monkey Grip one-hands the bastard sword"
d9d950fd195fc2b37ae42ec5d6548218441c0c6a  2026-09-05  fix: the script VM shift opcodes. "Make a script shift go the way it says (inc-gv1u)"
58d9f2ebbd026c6ff068b7accabcc666ec1b55d8  2026-09-04  docs: bead answers only. "resolve the 10 held questions from the overnight run"
dddec749dd5308d8484cae169c416a6ec9e73cac  2026-09-04  docs: bead activity only. "beads: park the tile work behind a libtcod 1.6.3 -> 1.24.0 upgrade"
0747c0cd7b9387b8b898e23f1dabc39a76467af6  2026-09-03  docs: bead activity only. "chore: bead activity for the fog render tint and the publication-gate hole (inc-qh0w, inc-m7xb)"
04431f2f073f861b1e33b67836e8cfd98c7c62ec  2026-09-02  graphics: trailer capture playback. "sdl,lib: -keys movement-script playback and -load for trailer capture"
